1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:01,760
Now it's time for the important part.

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:03,590
The crash animation.

3
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:08,360
Because if our crash doesn't look like a really epic, our players won't understand why the trees are

4
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,410
to be avoided.

5
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:14,240
So let's have a look at how we can enhance this game with a nice animation.

6
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:15,880
Let's get to it.

7
00:00:15,910 --> 00:00:21,910
So moving over to our player sprite, we can add in this when I receive player crashed broadcast.

8
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:28,240
So basically what we want to happen is for our player sprite to have a spin out effect when they touch

9
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,050
a tree.

10
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:34,990
And quite simply, all we need to do is go to the motions group and bring in this turn effect.

11
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:40,030
Then we can just repeat this say five times and giving this a go.

12
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,340
Skipping along until we hit a tree.

13
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:45,160
Ah well, that didn't quite work.

14
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:47,860
As you can see, it tries to turn, but it just turns back.

15
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:51,040
And also, even after we crashed, we can still ski left and right.

16
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:53,470
So let's see if we can fix that.

17
00:00:54,430 --> 00:01:00,430
Well, if you look closely, you will see that the problem is caused by this script here.

18
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:03,580
And to fix this problem is quite simple.

19
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:09,250
Basically, just like we did with the tree sprite, what we need to do is stop the other scripts.

20
00:01:09,250 --> 00:01:14,680
So grabbing a stop, all we can change it to stop other scripts in the sprite.

21
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:19,600
And this time, instead of putting it at the end of the script, we can add it to the start of the script.

22
00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:24,910
So again, giving that a play, you will see how much better that works.

23
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:30,130
Now we have a pretty nice animation that works when we crash, but I still think we can do better.

24
00:01:30,910 --> 00:01:37,690
So if you look down at our script, you can see that we turn by 15 degrees, which is fine and all,

25
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:39,730
but it does not look exactly smooth.

26
00:01:39,730 --> 00:01:42,880
So I'm going to do something a little sneaky here.

27
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:47,620
And instead of 15 I'm going to turn by movement speed.

28
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:53,650
Yes, I know this seems weird, but as you will see, it works when we give this a play.

29
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:56,590
Notice how much better that animation is.

30
00:01:57,110 --> 00:02:03,710
Now, the final thing to improve this even more is replace this repeat five times with a repeat until

31
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:04,370
block.

32
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:11,510
Now, just like we did with our other script, we can repeat until movement speed equals zero.

33
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:17,510
So just grab this equals block and this variable and set this to zero like that.

34
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:21,020
So giving that another go crashing into another tree.

35
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:24,830
Well, I think the results speak for themselves.

36
00:02:24,950 --> 00:02:28,280
Net looks like a remarkable crash.

